# Never translate line endings, for any file, in either direction.
#
# This is not a style preference. Qualification artifacts record a SHA-256 closure over the
# raw bytes of every .py file in the extension package, and the unit suite recomputes it and
# fails on a mismatch (see README, "Evidence is bound to source"). Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without this file a fresh clone on Windows
# would check the sources out with CRLF, change every byte hash, and turn the whole Phase 0
# curved-guide suite red against evidence that is in fact valid -- a failure that looks like
# a physics regression and is not one.
#
# Committing normalized LF is not enough on its own: it is the *checkout* direction that
# does the damage. "-text" disables both.
* -text

# Renders and captured frames are binary; keep diffs from trying to interpret them.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
